meta {
  name: Re-point the asset
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/library/{{libraryItemId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "asset_id": "{{abandonedAssetId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
}

docs {
  asset_id and owner_person_id are recorded when the item is created and cannot
  be changed afterwards.

  The reason is that everything downstream is keyed to the bytes. The indexed
  digest, the page ranges the placements in folder 11 record, and any citation
  a reader has already followed all describe one file. Swapping the file under
  a published item leaves every one of them pointing at pages that no longer
  say what they said, and nothing in the row would show that it had happened.
  A new edition is a new item, with supersedes_id naming the old one.
}
